type: software
title: "TCEP latitude analysis"
version: 1.1.0
date-released: 2026-09-20
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.22857802"
authors:
  - family-names: Liu
    given-names: Luyi
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0002-9443-1129"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/kelly-Liu44/TCEP-latitude-analysis"
abstract: >-
  Workflow for constructing a global tropical cyclone extreme precipitation
  (TCEP) event catalogue for 1980–2023 using MSWEP V2.8, IBTrACS V4, the tropical
  cyclone precipitation feature (TCPF) approach, and local wet-period
  99th-percentile thresholds. A frequency-weighted latitude-band decomposition
  separates annual mean intensity changes into latitudinal redistribution,
  within-latitude-band intensity change, and their interaction. The repository
  provides processing and analysis code, plotting scripts, and derived inputs
  for the manuscript figures and tables. Raw archives and complete intermediate
  catalogues are not redistributed.
keywords:
  - tropical cyclones
  - extreme precipitation
  - poleward migration
  - MSWEP
  - latitude decomposition
  - TCPF
